menu "Lab 3 (BME280)"

config LAB3_REG_SIM
    bool "Simulated BME280 registers (QEMU) instead of the I2C bus"
    default y
    help
        On (the default): main/bme280_i2c.c reads and writes the
        simulated register map of component bme280_regsim instead
        of the I2C bus, so the whole driver -- chip-id probe,
        calibration unpacking, compensation -- runs in QEMU, with
        fixed registers and known expected results.
        Off (sdkconfig.hw, build directory build-hw): the real
        sensor on the I2C bus, on the board.

endmenu
